  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Monday)\nIssued at 1235 PM CDT TUE SEP 15 2026\n\nOver the next few days, an anomalous ridge of high pressure will\ncontinue to limit opportunities for showers and thunderstorms\n(nil to very low chances) while prolonging above-normal\ntemperatures, reaching near record daily levels for a few\nlocations.\n\nFrom this weekend into next week, forecast models suggest that\nwhile the center/axis of the ridge of high pressure remains\nnearby, on its flank will exist a westward-drifting, upper-level\nlow near Florida and a shortwave trough/front over the Midwest.\nThese features may yield at least a modest uptick in shower and\nthunderstorm chances for parts of central Alabama from Sunday\nonward. At this time, the prospects of this being a pattern that\neases our (re)intensifying drought are low.\n\n89^GSatterwhite",
